[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to improper handling of file uploads, specifically a Denial of Service (DoS) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when the application does not impose adequate restrictions on the size or type of files that can be uploaded. If an attacker can upload excessively large zip files or files of unsupported types, it could lead to resource exhaustion on the server, causing it to become unresponsive or crash. This lack of validation and control over the input can allow malicious users to exploit the system by overwhelming it with large or numerous requests, thereby compromising the availability of the service.

